spans.s:
ṛtuka, adj. (ifc.) and subst. nt. (Pali -utuka, in sabbotuka),
(1) of, belonging to, a season: Divy 〔167.8〕 kālartukaiś (of the time and season) copakaranair anuvidhīyate; Mmk 〔27.21〕 yathartukena (text yathā˚) vā sugandhapuṣpeṇa;
(2) fruit of the season: Divy 〔531.5〕 (navaśasyāni navaphalāni) navartukāni; so MSV 〔i.7.6〕; Divy 〔531.8〕 navaiḥ phalaiḥ navaiḥ śasyakair navartukaiḥ.
